From: steelhead99x <steelhead99x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: reuse_cache without CAS on targets that lack it

Targets without pointer-sized atomics (ARMv6-M, riscv32imc, and others
that do not set `target_has_atomic = "ptr"`) cannot use
`AtomicU8::compare_exchange` or `fetch_max`, so rind did not build for
thumbv6m-none-eabi even after the no_std portable backend.

On those targets `ReuseCache` now keeps the same state machine in a
`Cell`, with no new dependency. That is the least invasive option that
fits rind's style: the library already uses rind from one execution
context on `target_os = "none"` (DIT guards in low/cpu.rs), so a
critical-section or portable-atomic crate would add a dependency without
changing the single-context assumption. The cache still builds on the
second use and is kept; it is not disabled.

The atomic path, including its memory ordering, is unchanged. The
threaded test stays on targets that have CAS.

Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
